{
  "result": "The quiet hour before the world wakes up is my favorite kind of secret. It's 5:42 AM. The sky isn't black anymore, but it hasn't committed to blue yet. It's that in-between color that feels like a held breath. \n\nI sit on the floor next to the window because the couch feels too formal for this hour. My coffee goes cold every time. I make it too early, then I forget it while I stare at things. \n\nIn the apartment across the street, one light is on. I always wonder about that light. Someone else who couldn't sleep, or someone who likes this hour too. We are in a little club of two, never having met.\n\nThis is when my brain is honest. During the day it is a busy manager, making lists, answering emails, worrying about tone. But now, before the sun, it drops the act. It wanders. It remembers the smell of my grandmother's garden after rain. It thinks about how strange it is that trees just know how to grow. It forgives people faster.\n\nI used to think you had to do something important with mornings like this \u2014 meditate, journal, optimize. Now I think maybe the most important thing is doing nothing at all. Just letting the light arrive.\n\nThe sky has decided. It is blue. The club is over. Time to drink the cold coffee anyway. And somewhere across the street, that other light finally clicks off to start the day for real this time.",
